# Engine files that include a shell header. Each line is a debt, not a
# permission: the gate fails on a NEW edge and fails again on an entry here that
# no longer happens, so a fixed edge cannot quietly stay listed.
#
# After B7 the zones are directories, so these are the edges that survived the
# move rather than an artefact of a name list.
#
# search.cpp -> uci.h        UCIEngine::wdl and format_score on the info line.
# search.cpp -> ucioption.h  Search::Worker holds const OptionsMap&; there is no
#                            way to drive a search without a process around it.
# timeman.cpp -> ucioption.h the time manager reads the clock-related options.
#                            Exposed BY the move: timeman is engine and
#                            ucioption is shell, which the old name lists put on
#                            the same side.
# types.h -> tune.h          DELIBERATE, and the only entry here that is not
#                            debt. Placed after types.h's own #endif so the SPSA
#                            macros reach anywhere types.h does.
search.cpp -> uci.h
search.cpp -> ucioption.h
timeman.cpp -> ucioption.h
types.h -> tune.h
